---
import Base from "@Layout/Base.astro";

import Related from "@Component/Related.astro";

import CodeFence from "@Component/CodeFence.astro";

import { ExternalLinks } from "@Library/Links";
---

<Base
	Title="SETUP // APHRODITE"
	Description="Install Aphrodite for Hermes Agent. Pick the plugin catalog, a git clone, cargo, or a source build. Includes Windows steps and how to confirm it works."
>
	<main
		class="relative z-10 mx-auto flex w-full max-w-[1440px] flex-col gap-24 px-5 py-32 sm:px-8 lg:gap-40 lg:px-14 lg:py-56"
	>
		<header class="relative flex w-full flex-col items-start">
			<div
				class="mb-5 -rotate-1 border border-black bg-raw-blood px-3 py-1 text-base font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-bone-white shadow-[3px_3px_0px_#000]"
			>
				SETUP
			</div>
			<h1
				class="font-headline text-3xl font-black uppercase tracking-tight text-bone-white drop-shadow-[4px_4px_0px_#520612] sm:text-5xl"
			>
				Install Aphrodite
			</h1>
			<p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl font-body text-base leading-relaxed text-bone-newsprint">
				Aphrodite is installed as a Hermes Agent plugin (recommended) or run as a
				standalone proxy for OpenAI-compatible APIs.
				<span class="mt-1 block text-base">Two things to know first: the plugin never
				downloads anything on its own - you run one setup command, and it fetches the
				Aphrodite binary and library from GitHub Releases, verifies them with SHA-256,
				and stores them in
				<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">~/.hermes/aphrodite/</code>.
				And you do not need Rust unless you build from source.</span>
				<span class="mt-1 block text-base">Not sure which to choose? Use the plugin
				catalog (Option 1).</span>
				<span class="mt-1 block text-base">The full host map, including the flavors still
				planned, is laid out on
				<a class="text-weathered-teal transition-colors hover:text-bone-white" href="/flavors/">FLAVORS</a>.</span>
			</p>
			<p class="mt-4 font-body text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-dust">
				WINDOWS: use PowerShell and run <code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">pwsh ./download.ps1</code>
				instead of <code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">bash download.sh</code> -
				the full Windows walkthrough is on
				<a class="text-weathered-teal underline transition-colors hover:text-bone-white" href="/docs/install/windows/">/docs/install/windows/</a>.
			</p>
		</header>

		<!-- OPTION 1: PLUGIN CATALOG -->
		<section class="relative w-full lg:w-5/6 lg:self-start">
			<div
				class="zine-box-crimson relative -rotate-[1.8deg] border-4 border-blood-crimson bg-carbon-void p-6 transition-transform duration-300 hover:rotate-0 sm:p-8"
			>
				<div
					class="absolute -top-3.5 left-6 border border-black bg-stamped-canary px-3 py-0.5 text-base font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-soot-black shadow-[2px_2px_0px_#000]"
				>
					#1 // PLUGIN CATALOG (RECOMMENDED)
				</div>
				<div class="mb-3 mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2">
					<h2 class="font-headline text-lg font-black uppercase text-bone-white sm:text-xl">
						Plugin catalog install
					</h2>
					<span class="text-base text-zinc-dust">5 STEPS</span>
				</div>
				<CodeFence
					Class="mb-3 border border-oxblood-dark [&>pre]:overflow-x-hidden [&>pre]:[overflow-wrap:anywhere]"
					Code={`$ hermes plugins install aphrodite
$ hermes plugins enable aphrodite // or answer yes at the Enable now? prompt
$ cd ~/.hermes/plugins/aphrodite
$ bash download.sh // or: pwsh ./download.ps1 - still required
$ hermes`}
				/>
				<div class="border-2 border-oxblood-dark bg-asphalt-panel p-3.5">
					<div class="mb-1 text-base font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-stamped-canary">
						OUTCOME // CATALOG INSTALL:
					</div>
					<div class="border border-oxblood-dark bg-soot-black p-2 font-mono text-base font-bold text-bone-white">
						Reviewed pinned checkout of the catalog entry, binaries fetched + SHA-256 verified, plugin enabled.
					</div>
					<div class="mt-3 border-l-4 border-stamped-canary bg-soot-black p-4">
						<div class="font-mono text-base font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-stamped-canary">
							THE CATALOG RULE
						</div>
						<p class="mt-2 font-body text-base leading-relaxed text-bone-newsprint">
							The catalog entry is reviewed and pinned -
							<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">hermes plugins install</code>
							checks out exactly that commit, never a branch tip. Do NOT run
							<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">aphrodite setup</code>
							in a catalog-managed directory - still run
							<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">download.sh</code>
							(or <code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">download.ps1</code>
							on Windows) from the installed plugin folder.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div class="mt-3 border-t border-oxblood-dark pt-3">
						<div class="font-mono text-base font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-weathered-teal">
							VERIFY IT WORKS
						</div>
						<p class="mt-2 font-body text-base leading-relaxed text-bone-newsprint">
							Start <code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">hermes</code>.
							The plugin should log that Aphrodite is enabled. If the binaries are
							missing, it logs the setup command and stays disabled until you run it.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div class="mt-2 font-mono text-base text-zinc-dust">
						SRC: <a class="text-weathered-teal underline transition-colors hover:text-bone-white" href={ExternalLinks.HermesGuide}>the Hermes plugin guide</a> - Installing from the catalog.
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- OPTION 2: GIT CLONE -->
		<section class="relative w-full lg:w-5/6 lg:self-end lg:-mt-12">
			<div
				class="zine-box-crimson relative -rotate-[2.2deg] border-4 border-blood-crimson bg-carbon-void p-6 transition-transform duration-300 hover:rotate-0 sm:p-8"
			>
				<div
					class="absolute -top-3.5 right-6 border border-black bg-stamped-canary px-3 py-0.5 text-base font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-soot-black shadow-[2px_2px_0px_#000]"
				>
					#2 // GIT CLONE (RECOMMENDED)
				</div>
				<div class="mb-3 mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-2">
					<h2 class="font-headline text-lg font-black uppercase text-bone-white sm:text-xl">
						Clone, link, download, enable
					</h2>
					<span class="text-base text-zinc-dust">7 STEPS</span>
				</div>
				<CodeFence
					Class="mb-3 border border-oxblood-dark [&>pre]:overflow-x-hidden [&>pre]:[overflow-wrap:anywhere]"
					Code={`$ git clone ${ExternalLinks.HermesRepository}.git
$ cd Aphrodite-Hermes
$ ln -s "$(pwd)" ~/.hermes/plugins/aphrodite
$ bash download.sh // or: pwsh ./download.ps1 (Windows)
$ cd ..
$ hermes plugins enable aphrodite
$ hermes`}
				/>
				<div class="border-2 border-oxblood-dark bg-asphalt-panel p-3.5">
					<div class="mb-1 text-base font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-stamped-canary">
						OUTCOME // VERIFIED INSTALL:
					</div>
					<div class="border border-oxblood-dark bg-soot-black p-2 font-mono text-base font-bold text-bone-white">
						Binary + native library (dylib) fetched from GitHub Releases, SHA-256 verified, plugin enabled.
					</div>
					<div class="mt-3 border-t border-oxblood-dark pt-3">
						<div class="font-mono text-base font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-weathered-teal">
							VERIFY IT WORKS
						</div>
						<p class="mt-2 font-body text-base leading-relaxed text-bone-newsprint">
							Start <code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">hermes</code>.
							The plugin should log that Aphrodite is enabled. If the binaries are
							missing, it logs the setup command and stays disabled until you run it.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- OPTION 3: CARGO -->
		<section class="relative w-full lg:w-5/6 lg:self-start">
			<div
				class="zine-box-crimson relative rotate-[2.2deg] border-4 border-blood-crimson bg-carbon-void p-6 transition-transform duration-300 hover:rotate-0 sm:p-8"
			>
				<div
					class="absolute -top-3.5 left-6 border border-black bg-raw-blood px-3 py-0.5 text-base font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-bone-white shadow-[2px_2px_0px_#000]"
				>
					#3 // CARGO
				</div>
				<h2 class="mb-3 mt-2 font-headline text-lg font-black uppercase text-bone-white sm:text-xl">
					Crates.io install
				</h2>
				<CodeFence
					Class="mb-3 border border-oxblood-dark [&>pre]:overflow-x-hidden [&>pre]:[overflow-wrap:anywhere]"
					Code={`$ cargo install aphrodite // proxy binary
$ cargo install aphrodite-hermes // dylib + helper bin
$ aphrodite setup`}
				/>
				<div class="mb-3 font-mono text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-dust">
					// cargo installs the binaries only - aphrodite setup then writes a minimal
					// loader into ~/.hermes/plugins/aphrodite. For the full plugin, use Option 1
					// or 2. Needs Rust 1.88+ (the repo toolchain pins nightly).
				</div>
				<div class="border-t border-oxblood-dark pt-3">
					<div class="font-mono text-base font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-weathered-teal">
						VERIFY IT WORKS
					</div>
					<p class="mt-2 font-body text-base leading-relaxed text-bone-newsprint">
						Option 3 does not install the plugin by itself - after
						<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">aphrodite setup</code>
						writes the loader, start <code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">hermes</code>.
						The plugin should log that Aphrodite is enabled; if the binaries are missing,
						it logs the setup command and stays disabled until you run it.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- OPTION 4: FROM SOURCE -->
		<section class="relative w-full lg:w-5/6 lg:self-end lg:-mt-12">
			<div
				class="zine-box-crimson relative rotate-[1.4deg] border-4 border-blood-crimson bg-carbon-void p-6 transition-transform duration-300 hover:rotate-0 sm:p-8"
			>
				<div
					class="absolute -top-3.5 right-6 border border-black bg-weathered-teal px-3 py-0.5 text-base font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-bone-white shadow-[2px_2px_0px_#000]"
				>
					#4 // FROM SOURCE
				</div>
				<h2 class="mb-3 mt-2 font-headline text-lg font-black uppercase text-bone-white sm:text-xl">
					Build it yourself
				</h2>
				<CodeFence
					Class="mb-3 border border-oxblood-dark [&>pre]:overflow-x-hidden [&>pre]:[overflow-wrap:anywhere]"
					Code={`$ git clone ${ExternalLinks.Repository}.git
$ cd Aphrodite
$ git submodule update --init --recursive
$ cargo build --release -p aphrodite -p aphrodite-hermes`}
				/>
				<div class="mb-3 font-mono text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-dust">
					// needs Rust 1.88+ (the repo toolchain pins nightly). The build outputs land
					// in target/release/ - point APHRODITE_BINARY_PATH / APHRODITE_HERMES_DYLIB_PATH
					// at them, or copy them into ~/.hermes/aphrodite/binaries/.
				</div>
				<div class="border-t border-oxblood-dark pt-3">
					<div class="font-mono text-base font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-weathered-teal">
						VERIFY IT WORKS
					</div>
					<p class="mt-2 font-body text-base leading-relaxed text-bone-newsprint">
						Start <code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">hermes</code>.
						The plugin should log that Aphrodite is enabled. If the binaries are
						missing, it logs the setup command and stays disabled until you run it.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- PROXY // THE STANDALONE LANE -->
		<section class="relative w-full lg:w-3/4 lg:self-start">
			<div
				class="zine-box-crimson relative rotate-[1.6deg] border-4 border-blood-crimson bg-carbon-void p-6 transition-transform duration-300 hover:rotate-0 sm:p-8"
			>
				<div
					class="absolute -top-3.5 left-6 border border-black bg-weathered-teal px-3 py-0.5 text-base font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-bone-white shadow-[2px_2px_0px_#000]"
				>
					PROXY // THE STANDALONE LANE
				</div>
				<h2 class="mb-3 mt-2 font-headline text-lg font-black uppercase text-bone-white sm:text-xl">
					Run it without Hermes
				</h2>
				<p class="font-body text-base leading-relaxed text-bone-newsprint">
					The same compression engine runs as a standalone proxy: point any
					OpenAI-compatible client's
					<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">base_url</code> at
					<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">http://localhost:9798</code>
					(token) or <code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">:9797</code>
					(cache), and responses compress over plain HTTP. Invoked without an
					<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">aphrodite.toml</code>,
					the binary needs
					<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">--api-key</code> or
					<code class="font-mono text-base text-weathered-teal">APHRODITE_API_KEY</code>.
				</p>
				<p class="mt-3 font-body text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-dust">
					The full surface is documented on the proxy pages:
					<a class="text-weathered-teal underline transition-colors hover:text-bone-white" href="/docs/proxy/architecture/">architecture</a>,
					<a class="text-weathered-teal underline transition-colors hover:text-bone-white" href="/docs/proxy/compression/">compression</a>,
					<a class="text-weathered-teal underline transition-colors hover:text-bone-white" href="/docs/proxy/handlers/">handlers</a>,
					<a class="text-weathered-teal underline transition-colors hover:text-bone-white" href="/docs/proxy/retry/">retry</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- CONFIG TOML MODULE -->
		<section class="relative w-full lg:w-3/4 lg:self-end lg:-mt-10">
			<div
				class="zine-box-crimson relative -rotate-[2.5deg] border-4 border-blood-crimson bg-carbon-void p-6 transition-transform duration-300 hover:rotate-0 sm:p-8"
			>
				<div
					class="absolute -top-3.5 right-6 border border-black bg-weathered-teal px-3 py-0.5 text-base font-black uppercase tracking-widest text-bone-white shadow-[2px_2px_0px_#000]"
				>
					/CONFIG.TOML
				</div>
				<h2 class="mb-3 mt-2 font-headline text-lg font-black uppercase text-bone-white sm:text-xl">
					Configuration
				</h2>
				<div class="space-y-1 border border-oxblood-dark bg-soot-black p-4 font-mono text-base text-bone-newsprint">
					<div class="text-weathered-teal"># resolution order:</div>
					<div>./aphrodite.toml <span class="text-zinc-dust">then</span> ~/.hermes/aphrodite/aphrodite.toml</div>
					<div class="pt-2 text-weathered-teal"># precedence:</div>
					<div>env var <span class="text-zinc-dust">&gt;</span> TOML <span class="text-zinc-dust">&gt;</span> default</div>
					<div class="pt-2 text-weathered-teal">[compression]</div>
					<div>auto_reload = <span class="text-stamped-canary">false</span> <span class="text-zinc-dust"># opt-in</span></div>
					<div class="pt-2 text-weathered-teal">[flow]</div>
					<div>budget_chars = <span class="text-stamped-canary">2600</span> <span class="text-zinc-dust"># hard cap per turn</span></div>
				</div>
				<div class="mt-4 flex items-center justify-between border-t border-oxblood-dark pt-2 text-base text-zinc-dust">
					<span>TEMPLATES IN THE REPO:</span>
					<span class="font-bold text-stamped-canary">aphrodite.toml.example + the embedded template</span>
				</div>
				<p class="mt-2 font-body text-base leading-relaxed text-zinc-dust">
					Two shipped files stay in sync: aphrodite.toml.example (the annotated reference)
					and the embedded template the binary ships with. Keys not yet wired into the
					runtime are annotated DOCUMENTED BUT UNWIRED in the example - it is the source
					of truth for the documented surface.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- RELATED: the natural neighbors -->
		<Related
			Links={[
				{ Href: "/plugin/", Label: "PLUGIN" },
				{ Href: "/hermes/", Label: "HERMES" },
				{ Href: "/hooks/", Label: "HOOKS" },
				{ Href: "/flavors/", Label: "FLAVORS" },
				{ Href: "/docs/", Label: "DOCS" },
			]}
		/>
	</main>
</Base>